 2. 🤖 Prepping for cyber doomsday 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 First three items on the British government's National Resilience Checklist. Screenshot: GOV.UK 

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The governments of the U.S. and Britain are suddenly making old-school preparations for the possibility of a cyber-triggered long-term blackout:

 The Pentagon is "preparing U.S. military bases to keep operating for at least 90 days without outside support as it prepares for the possibility of a major war that could cripple power grids, disrupt supply chains and threaten critical infrastructure on American soil," Fox News Digital reports . Under a broader military initiative called FORTRESS, "every major military installation in the continental United States would be expected to sustain essential operations independently for at least 90 days, including access to electricity, water, fuel and communications." The British government urged the public to keep three days of emergency supplies at home, including water and canned goods ("tinned" for the Brits). The "Be Ready" campaign was triggered by the PHP software vulnerability exposed last week, plus a record-setting summer of heat, drought and wildfires. 😬 Between the lines: If you marinate online, you're being barraged with warnings of a cyber-induced Black October.

 Mike Cernovich, an influential pro-Trump voice on X, posted yesterday : "Something is coming. You can sense it." 
 
