 4. 🗳️ Early &#x27;28 contenders 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Chart: The New York Times Democrats' 2028 race is wide open: Kamala Harris leads with just 12% of primary voters, and 45% didn't name a favorite, a New York Times/Siena telephone poll of Democratic primary voters found. 

 Republican primary voters are coalescing around either Vice President Vance (33%) or Secretary of State Marco Rubio (23%) . 8% of Republicans named Trump himself, even though he's ineligible. Keep reading (gift link) ... Explore the data . 

 
 
