 6. 🇧🇷 Brazil election shocker: Lula the survivor 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva addresses supporters last night during a victory celebration on Paulista Avenue in São Paulo, Brazil. Photo: Natacha Pisarenko/AP Ending a string of conservative victories in Latin America, Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva, a leftist critic of President Trump, pulled off a stunning comeback to cling to power over right-wing Flávio Bolsonaro.

 Bolsonaro, the son of imprisoned ex-president Jair Bolsonaro, refused to concede and said he'll ask to have the result annulled. Why it matters: Lula's victory ( 52% ) is a blow to Brazil's right-wing populist movement and preserves a major counterweight to Trump's influence in Latin America, Axios' Rebecca Falconer writes. 

 🔭 Zoom in: Brazil's electoral court announced that Lula, who turns 81 tomorrow, held an unassailable lead of nearly 4.4 million votes over opponent Bolsonaro.

