 7. 💰 Big Tech legal bills pile up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A tidal wave of litigation is catching up to Meta, leading to $42 billion in recent penalties and settlements . It's a powerful reminder to AI companies that they could face a reckoning in court even when regulation lags, Axios AI &amp; tech managing editor Bradley Olson writes. 

 Why it matters : AI companies are racing to build better models and autonomous agents, but they don't enjoy the same legal protections that shielded web platforms for decades. Meta's big bills offer a preview of potential legal exposure. After a $25 billion penalty in a New Mexico data privacy case this past week, Meta chief legal officer C.J. Mahoney said : "At its core, this lawsuit seeks to impose a tax on speech to enforce new rules for what people can say online."

